WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:16.400
Today, celebrating Shri Krishna Puja, is a
very joyous day. One of the things is,

2
00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:27.680
when people get very serious, you need the
play of Shri Krishna —

3
00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:35.280
because even in Sahaja Yoga we get very
serious, worried about this chakra,

4
00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:41.920
worried about that chakra, and we get very
serious about the whole thing.

5
00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:48.560
This puja was in Delhi. Before the puja it
was the start of Holi,

6
00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:54.960
and it was at the old ashram in
Safdarjung, around 1985, I think.

7
00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:06.320
We assembled at the Safdarjung Ashram, and
Shri Mataji saw we were all very serious.

8
00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:12.240
This was more or less the start of Sahaja
Yoga in Delhi, in the early '80s —

9
00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:15.920
we had just sort of got to know about the
chakras and how to clear them,

10
00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:18.880
and we were always trying to improve them.

11
00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:22.560
If things weren't going well we'd feel
very disappointed.

12
00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:25.680
So everybody was very serious.

13
00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:32.240
And, you know, when everybody becomes too
serious, she becomes playful —

14
00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:38.800
her expression suddenly turned very
joyful, Krishna-like.

15
00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:43.040
Out of the blue, she started asking
everybody, "Who's your friend?

16
00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:51.280
Who's your friend?" We looked at each
other. Someone said, "All are my friends."

17
00:01:51.280 --> 00:01:53.520
"All are? No — one, you tell me."

18
00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:54.320
"Everybody."

19
00:01:54.320 --> 00:01:57.920
"No, no, I don't believe you.

20
00:01:57.920 --> 00:02:02.389
First start with one friend, then with
two, then with three.

21
00:02:02.389 --> 00:02:05.600
If you say 'all,' it is lost. Let's see —

22
00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:11.680
there is one friend of mine, start it like
that.

23
00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:16.320
This is just a crowd saying 'all are your
friends.'"

24
00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:20.230
Obviously nobody had thought of it that
way —

25
00:02:20.230 --> 00:02:23.200
each just answered "so-and-so." Somebody
said, "No,

26
00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:28.720
so-and-so." Basically these were the
organizers, the leaders,

27
00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:33.840
and she was trying to make them
understand:

28
00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:39.600
you are totally focused on organizing, on
administration,

29
00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:44.400
but you don't connect with people — so you
don't have any friends.

30
00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:51.600
So she asked the coordinator, "Who's your
friend? Who is your friend, Subramanyam?"

31
00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:56.560
"No, no — forget about me, I am like a
bubble."

32
00:02:59.840 --> 00:03:05.600
"How many friends have you got here? Let's
see —

33
00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:08.240
no, no, not an enemy's name, a friend's."

34
00:03:08.240 --> 00:03:11.440
The person was totally surprised.

35
00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:46.400
She then explained what makes a friend:
"What is the criteria? Let's see —

36
00:03:46.400 --> 00:04:02.640
the criteria of a friend is this: even if
I challenge you,

37
00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:10.240
suppose I tell you something against, say,
your friend Yogi Mahajan —

38
00:04:10.240 --> 00:04:20.640
if you support that, then you are not his
friend." That's what she found:

39
00:04:20.640 --> 00:04:26.800
real friends support each other through
thick and thin.

40
00:04:26.800 --> 00:04:30.000
That's the kind of friendship she meant.

41
00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:38.320
"I like people who support the Sahaja
Yogis, who come forward and say, 'Mother,

42
00:04:38.320 --> 00:04:41.360
please forgive him — he did some mistake,
I know,

43
00:04:41.360 --> 00:04:47.760
but please forgive him.' I feel very happy
about that. We are collective —

44
00:04:47.760 --> 00:04:54.160
like a collective, you are all born
together, so you help each other."

45
00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:58.880
But what happens is, new people come,

46
00:04:58.880 --> 00:05:05.120
and then they go back to whatever they
were doing before,

47
00:05:05.120 --> 00:05:08.640
and people discourage them: "Why are you
doing all this?

48
00:05:09.280 --> 00:05:11.360
Why not do something else — there's this
happening,

49
00:05:11.360 --> 00:05:16.960
that happening." But if a bond has
developed, a friendship has developed,

50
00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:25.120
you can lift them back — you can talk to
them, you can explain things to them.

51
00:05:25.120 --> 00:05:31.360
So why do we lose so many people? A lot of
people come to public programs,

52
00:05:31.360 --> 00:05:36.640
they attend the center for a while, and
then after six months they disappear,

53
00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:40.800
because something or other diverted them,

54
00:05:40.800 --> 00:05:48.800
and there was nobody who could be called a
friend — someone who would pull them back.

55
00:05:48.800 --> 00:05:55.440
Likewise, when you have problems at your
office, or sometimes domestic problems,

56
00:05:55.440 --> 00:06:00.000
and you're down, you might think, "I've
been doing Sahaja Yoga so long —

57
00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:03.440
why is this happening to me?" You get
depressed.

58
00:06:03.440 --> 00:06:06.160
But if you have a group of friends,
they'll come and cheer you up —

59
00:06:06.160 --> 00:06:12.000
whether your mind has moved to the left or
to the right,

60
00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:14.240
they bring you back to balance.

61
00:06:14.240 --> 00:06:19.440
So it is very important, she said, that
you have friends,

62
00:06:19.440 --> 00:06:25.440
because they are your support system. If
you don't have them, you are lonely —

63
00:06:25.440 --> 00:06:39.600
people who don't befriend anybody, or whom
nobody befriends, remain lonely and lost.

64
00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:44.960
So even when new people come to the
center, try to befriend them,

65
00:06:44.960 --> 00:06:53.200
talk to them, invite them over.

66
00:06:55.040 --> 00:07:09.120
In Sahaj Dharma we are collective beings,

67
00:07:10.800 --> 00:07:28.480
and we stand by each other even in front
of our Mother — that's friendship.

68
00:07:28.480 --> 00:07:34.640
You support each other, you help each
other: "Please forgive him, Mother —

69
00:07:34.640 --> 00:07:40.080
he might have made a mistake, please help
him, Mother." That, she said,

70
00:07:40.080 --> 00:07:44.880
she loved the most of all. Instead, nobody
invites anybody —

71
00:07:44.880 --> 00:07:50.800
you just meet at the center, and that's
it. So how do you bond?

72
00:07:50.800 --> 00:07:55.120
"I am very happy," she said, "that you in
Bombay have a small group that is bonding,

73
00:07:55.120 --> 00:08:01.200
and that will bring in more people, and it
goes on." What is it? Love.

74
00:08:02.240 --> 00:08:12.240
She then mentioned that, since Holi was
there, Shri Krishna wanted to play Holi —

75
00:08:12.240 --> 00:08:15.600
and that's why he created Vrindavan,
that's why he created all these worlds,

76
00:08:15.600 --> 00:08:18.640
because he can't play alone.

77
00:08:18.640 --> 00:08:30.960
You can't have a party alone, you need
friends, you can't enjoy alone.

78
00:08:43.600 --> 00:08:48.040
"Venugopal, find your friend, and now
we'll have a bhai bandhan.

79
00:08:48.040 --> 00:08:53.840
Yogi Mahajan, you too. Rakhi bandhan is
fine — that's for a safe married life —

80
00:08:53.840 --> 00:08:58.640
but what about bhai bandhan? So today we
decide, in Sahaja Yoga,

81
00:08:58.640 --> 00:09:01.520
we will all have a bhai bandhan, to begin
with."

82
00:09:01.520 --> 00:09:04.480
Then — how many "bhais" you'll have isn't
the point.

83
00:09:04.480 --> 00:09:07.280
First you have one bhai, start with
one.

84
00:09:07.840 --> 00:09:10.400
You don't have eleven children all
together, isn't?

85
00:09:11.280 --> 00:09:15.680
So you can have one brother, then another
brother —

86
00:09:15.680 --> 00:09:20.480
I can't have all the brothers together.
If that's going to happen,

87
00:09:20.480 --> 00:09:25.200
you must start with one friend, then a
second friend, then a third.

88
00:09:38.936 --> 00:10:27.780
[Marathi]

89
00:10:28.217 --> 00:10:32.402
This is how the whole creation took place -

90
00:10:32.589 --> 00:10:40.480
the Absolute wanted to enjoy his own
reflection, so he created Prakriti,

91
00:10:40.480 --> 00:10:44.160
and Prakriti created the creation.

92
00:10:44.160 --> 00:10:51.120
So unless there is love, how are you going
to enjoy anything? Of course,

93
00:10:51.120 --> 00:10:55.040
when we were there, we could feel her
presence,

94
00:10:55.040 --> 00:10:58.480
and there was so much joy and love coming
from her.

95
00:10:58.480 --> 00:11:09.600
But without seeing her, how will they feel
her love? Through you —

96
00:11:09.600 --> 00:11:20.240
that is the magnet that will keep them
within the gravity of Sahaja Yoga.

97
00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:24.960
How is she going to express her love
through this new generation,

98
00:11:24.960 --> 00:11:26.560
who have never seen her?

99
00:11:26.560 --> 00:11:33.920
She expresses it through you, through your
Kundalini, and then they feel it.

100
00:11:33.920 --> 00:11:40.640
There's a very interesting story of a Sufi
saint.

101
00:11:41.600 --> 00:11:51.840
God was very pleased with his devotion, so
he said to him,

102
00:11:51.840 --> 00:11:59.840
"Ask what you want." The Sufi said, "Make
me like a prophet —

103
00:11:59.840 --> 00:12:04.640
Prophet Muhammad." God said, "But I have
already created Prophet Muhammad,

104
00:12:04.640 --> 00:12:08.960
I can't make another Prophet Muhammad." So
he said, "Okay,

105
00:12:08.960 --> 00:12:14.720
then make me like Hazrat Ali." God said,
"I have already made Hazrat Ali —

106
00:12:14.720 --> 00:12:19.120
how can I make another Hazrat Ali?" So the
Sufi said, "Okay,

107
00:12:19.120 --> 00:12:23.360
then I don't want anything." God said,
"No, no —

108
00:12:23.360 --> 00:12:29.520
what I will bless you with is that the
fragrance of Prophet Muhammad,

109
00:12:29.520 --> 00:12:31.280
the fragrance of Hazrat Ali,

110
00:12:31.280 --> 00:12:37.280
will come through you." So they will not
have met Shri Mataji,

111
00:12:37.280 --> 00:12:42.480
but the fragrance of Shri Mataji will come
through you,

112
00:12:42.480 --> 00:12:48.400
and they will feel her through you.

113
00:12:48.400 --> 00:12:55.760
So it's all right to do pujas, to do all
the rituals —

114
00:12:55.760 --> 00:13:04.880
but unless you see other people as the
Spirit,

115
00:13:04.880 --> 00:13:12.360
unless you feel the Kundalini of other
people, it doesn't work.

116
00:13:12.360 --> 00:13:17.360
If you're only bothered all the time about
"what is happening to me" and not

117
00:13:17.360 --> 00:13:22.720
concerned about that person and what you
do for others, that's not enough.

118
00:13:22.720 --> 00:13:30.880
Shri Mataji once told us a story about a
devotee of Shri Krishna.

119
00:13:30.880 --> 00:13:36.160
There was a saint in Maharashtra —

120
00:13:36.160 --> 00:13:50.791
people used to carry water in a container
all the way to a temple of Shri Krishna in

121
00:13:50.791 --> 00:13:58.240
Gujarat. That was regarded as a great act
of surrender to Shri Krishna.

122
00:13:58.240 --> 00:14:04.640
This saint also carried water in that
container, covered,

123
00:14:06.240 --> 00:14:13.280
all the way from his village in
Maharashtra.

124
00:14:13.280 --> 00:14:23.440
When he reached the temple, at the foot of
it he saw a donkey —

125
00:14:23.440 --> 00:14:35.200
very thirsty, dying of thirst — and he
gave the water to the donkey.

126
00:14:35.200 --> 00:14:40.000
Everybody said, "Imagine — you carried
this water for miles, for days,

127
00:14:41.200 --> 00:14:49.520
to offer to the deity here, and now you've
given it to this donkey!" He said,

128
00:14:49.520 --> 00:14:51.120
"You don't know —

129
00:14:51.120 --> 00:15:02.640
God has come all the way down here to take
the water." That's the attitude he took.

130
00:15:02.640 --> 00:15:08.880
So for a self-realized person, the
compassion should be like that —

131
00:15:08.880 --> 00:15:15.520
of a very generous nature. If you are not
generous, if you are miserly,

132
00:15:15.520 --> 00:15:32.080
always worried about your money and saving
it, then you are not a mature Sahaja Yogi.

133
00:15:34.400 --> 00:15:40.640
Miserliness is against the Spirit — the
Spirit is extremely generous,

134
00:15:44.160 --> 00:15:54.120
it never tries to save something, or cheat
people, or steal —

135
00:15:54.120 --> 00:16:04.080
that's out of the question. There's no
greed at all.

136
00:16:07.520 --> 00:16:16.320
A realized soul cannot be greedy; it has
to be extremely generous.

137
00:16:16.320 --> 00:16:21.520
So it's about how you see, how you
perceive.

138
00:16:21.520 --> 00:16:29.840
If you're not kind to others and say, "No,
no, my attention is only on Shri Mataji,

139
00:16:29.840 --> 00:16:31.600
I'm not bothered about the rest" —

140
00:16:31.600 --> 00:16:36.880
that's not how it works, because they are
her children, they are her creation.

141
00:16:36.880 --> 00:16:42.160
If you're kind to them — say you're the
one who always does the aarti at puja,

142
00:16:43.280 --> 00:16:47.000
but there's someone who's never done it, a
new person —

143
00:16:47.520 --> 00:16:53.600
give them a chance, since you've already
done it. Give others a chance.

144
00:16:53.600 --> 00:16:57.240
That's how Australia has come up — they
help each other.

145
00:16:57.240 --> 00:17:03.120
Have you heard about their music of joy?
With their own funds —

146
00:17:03.120 --> 00:17:06.240
they're all working people, they take time
off —

147
00:17:06.240 --> 00:17:12.160
they go to countries where no work has
been done before on Sahaja Yoga,

148
00:17:12.160 --> 00:17:24.720
and they spread Sahaja Yoga through music,&nbsp;

149
00:17:28.560 --> 00:17:34.960
going to remote places. This is love.

150
00:17:34.960 --> 00:17:37.840
They don't know anybody there. Like last
year, they went to Bihar —

151
00:17:37.840 --> 00:17:41.280
they didn't know anybody there, and Bihar
is a very remote place in India;

152
00:17:41.280 --> 00:17:44.640
everybody likes to go to the big cities
where the connectivity is,

153
00:17:45.360 --> 00:17:47.920
but they went to remote places.

154
00:17:47.920 --> 00:17:57.120
I'm talking about the year '95. Sahaja
Yoga was mainly in Maharashtra,

155
00:17:57.120 --> 00:18:01.360
North India, a little in the South, a
little in Calcutta —

156
00:18:01.360 --> 00:18:08.080
we hadn't gone to the East at all, Assam
and all those areas.

157
00:18:11.040 --> 00:18:18.240
I was thinking about how to go there,
because we didn't have enough resources,

158
00:18:18.240 --> 00:18:25.840
not enough manpower. So I was talking to
the Australians, and they said,

159
00:18:25.840 --> 00:18:34.320
"We'll go there." Can you imagine? Twenty
of them came all the way from Australia,

160
00:18:34.320 --> 00:18:38.080
went to Assam, to Nagaland, all those
places,

161
00:18:38.080 --> 00:18:42.240
and stayed there for a month spreading
Sahaja Yoga.

162
00:18:42.240 --> 00:18:45.600
That's when our first centers there
started.

163
00:18:45.600 --> 00:18:47.440
When Shri Mataji heard about it,

164
00:18:47.440 --> 00:18:57.120
she was very pleased that the Australians
had done such work,

165
00:18:57.120 --> 00:19:02.080
and that's why she always praised the
Australians so much —

166
00:19:02.080 --> 00:19:07.600
the country of Shri Ganesha. That is what
pleases her more —

167
00:19:07.600 --> 00:19:13.680
when you do something for somebody, she
feels pleased.

168
00:19:13.680 --> 00:19:19.520
She also always said the Germans came to
Russia to help spread Sahaja Yoga,

169
00:19:19.520 --> 00:19:23.120
and that stayed with her — it pleased her
very much.

170
00:19:30.400 --> 00:19:38.080
I think she was attracted by this because
the Germans have realized that whatever

171
00:19:38.080 --> 00:19:50.200
they did was absolutely inhuman, and I was
so happy to see, when I went to Russia,

172
00:19:50.200 --> 00:20:00.960
that the people who came to give
realizations were mostly Germans.

173
00:20:00.960 --> 00:20:08.480
It really makes you feel tender about the
whole thing,

174
00:20:08.480 --> 00:20:12.560
that the Germans felt it was important —

175
00:20:12.560 --> 00:20:19.920
they were the ones attracted to come to
Russia to give realization to Russians.

176
00:20:19.920 --> 00:20:29.800
And you must know, the number of Russians
killed was the greatest in the world —

177
00:20:30.640 --> 00:20:34.000
by the Germans.

178
00:20:34.000 --> 00:20:38.800
So the Goddess is always pleased when you
do something for others.

179
00:20:38.800 --> 00:20:43.834
She's not concerned with how much you
donate, how much money you give —

180
00:20:43.834 --> 00:20:50.000
she's concerned with what you do for
others, and without seeking credit,

181
00:20:50.000 --> 00:20:54.080
without your name being on it.

182
00:20:54.080 --> 00:20:57.600
People give, people do, but then they want
their name: "Okay,

183
00:20:57.600 --> 00:20:59.920
we'll give this much donation for the
ashram,

184
00:20:59.920 --> 00:21:02.400
but our name should be on the room,

185
00:21:02.400 --> 00:21:14.560
donated by so-and-so." That is when you go
beyond the Agnya and enjoy the Sahasrara —

186
00:21:14.560 --> 00:21:23.840
you yourself enjoy your own Self,&nbsp;&nbsp;

187
00:21:28.800 --> 00:21:32.800
the Atma
by the Atma.

188
00:21:32.800 --> 00:21:37.760
And the Atma also enjoys the Atma, through
the Atma.

189
00:21:37.760 --> 00:21:43.280
That's why she said it's not happiness,
it's joy — joy that is beyond happiness.

190
00:21:43.280 --> 00:21:47.440
The joy is from your Atma.

191
00:21:47.440 --> 00:21:53.360
A person whose Atma is joy is not bothered
about anything,

192
00:21:54.320 --> 00:22:00.000
because he himself is the joy, and
wherever he goes he gives joy —

193
00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:02.560
that's his nature, he's not doing anyone a
favor.

194
00:22:04.240 --> 00:22:11.120
It's his nature, like it's the flower's
nature to give fragrance.

195
00:22:11.120 --> 00:22:19.600
This is the kind of joy we have to feel.

196
00:22:19.600 --> 00:22:23.720
If you're not feeling joy in Sahaja Yoga,
then you've missed something —

197
00:22:25.200 --> 00:22:27.680
maybe you're too serious,

198
00:22:27.680 --> 00:22:30.960
maybe you're too worried about whether
you'll "get there." If the joy is in your

199
00:22:30.960 --> 00:22:39.280
heart, it's there in you all the time, you
don't have to be technical about it.

200
00:22:39.280 --> 00:22:46.320
And even if it's not there, she is there
in your heart, so it doesn't matter —

201
00:22:46.320 --> 00:22:51.440
it will come, it will go, it will come, it
will go, and then it will learn to stay.

202
00:22:51.440 --> 00:22:55.520
That's how Sahaja Yoga is.

203
00:22:55.520 --> 00:23:10.000
So, now, if you have any questions, you
can ask.

204
00:23:10.000 --> 00:23:15.680
Yes.

205
00:23:40.720 --> 00:23:48.400
What has happened is, all the protagonists
in the books I've written are real people,

206
00:23:48.400 --> 00:23:57.920
but with different names. I've observed
people from different walks of life —

207
00:23:57.920 --> 00:24:05.520
some are artists, some are musicians, some
are bankers, some are businessmen.

208
00:24:07.280 --> 00:24:13.840
When I saw them coming to Sahaja Yoga, I
had doubts:

209
00:24:13.840 --> 00:24:19.040
how can people with this kind of
background get their realization?

210
00:24:19.040 --> 00:24:27.920
They're so self-centered, or so
competitive, or aggressive. And then,

211
00:24:27.920 --> 00:24:34.640
over the years, I observed how Shri Mataji
worked on them,

212
00:24:34.640 --> 00:24:43.440
and how they suddenly emerged glorious —
jai!

213
00:24:43.440 --> 00:24:48.400
So it inspired me to write about them,

214
00:24:48.400 --> 00:24:55.840
and that's how I changed their names and
changed the background,

215
00:24:56.400 --> 00:25:02.240
but the reality was the same. So when you
read it,

216
00:25:02.240 --> 00:25:10.560
and it's something that's actually
happened, you connect with it —

217
00:25:10.560 --> 00:25:12.800
you get the same experience.

218
00:25:12.800 --> 00:25:20.000
That's the resonance of somebody else
getting a realization,

219
00:25:20.000 --> 00:25:23.200
and through that you also feel the
vibration.

220
00:25:23.200 --> 00:25:30.320
I'll tell you a very interesting story. It
was our first year in Calcutta.

221
00:25:32.800 --> 00:25:39.840
We were staying at the Park Hotel — Shri
Mataji's room was on the fourth floor,

222
00:25:40.560 --> 00:25:47.520
ours was on the second floor, and there
were just five or six of us volunteers,

223
00:25:48.800 --> 00:25:51.760
sitting and talking.

224
00:25:55.440 --> 00:26:00.960
The owner of the hotel came up and said,
"Mother, please give me realization."

225
00:26:00.960 --> 00:26:09.120
Suddenly all six of us felt a jump — like
the Kundalini just shot up.

226
00:26:09.120 --> 00:26:10.080
We looked at each other:

227
00:26:10.080 --> 00:26:14.160
"Maybe something's happened to him." We
asked each other, "Did something —?" "No,

228
00:26:14.160 --> 00:26:17.600
no, nothing, I'm just talking to you." And
I said,

229
00:26:17.600 --> 00:26:22.560
"Something has happened on the fourth
floor, where Shri Mataji is —

230
00:26:22.560 --> 00:26:27.520
let's go running." So we went running, and
when he got his realization,

231
00:26:27.520 --> 00:26:30.880
everyone came running from their rooms.
"What's happened?

232
00:26:30.880 --> 00:26:33.040
We're feeling so joyous!"

233
00:26:33.040 --> 00:26:38.880
Shri Mataji was laughing, and there was
this person sitting on the floor,

234
00:26:38.880 --> 00:26:46.240
and she said, "See the vibrations of this
man, feel the vibrations." And we saw —

235
00:26:46.240 --> 00:26:49.280
his Kundalini had come up.

236
00:26:49.280 --> 00:26:54.640
They stood there for at least half an
hour, enjoying him, and he enjoying them.

237
00:26:54.640 --> 00:26:59.360
No thought passed. They didn't know he was
the owner of the hotel,

238
00:26:59.360 --> 00:27:04.160
and he didn't know who they were, or from
what part of the country —

239
00:27:04.160 --> 00:27:08.160
and he just shot up like that. And we
said, "Yes, this is it."

240
00:27:08.160 --> 00:27:13.320
So it happened somewhere else, but we
experienced it too — it's the same thing.

241
00:27:13.320 --> 00:27:18.000
That pure joy of humanity that Confucius
described —

242
00:27:18.000 --> 00:27:24.880
the real, true friendship of purity. But
when there is lust, greed,

243
00:27:24.880 --> 00:27:36.240
and selfish thought, it ends in miserable
tragedies. So one must know:

244
00:27:36.240 --> 00:27:37.760
for the first time,

245
00:27:37.760 --> 00:27:43.120
a rapport is established among human
beings on a very pure level.

246
00:27:43.120 --> 00:27:48.080
Things may be happening in Australia while
we're sitting here,

247
00:27:48.080 --> 00:27:50.720
but if we're connected to her —

248
00:27:50.720 --> 00:27:55.600
through her the Australians are connected,
and through her we are connected.

249
00:27:55.600 --> 00:28:01.440
So if she's pleased, suddenly, out of the
blue, you feel very nice vibrations,

250
00:28:01.440 --> 00:28:03.520
sitting there doing nothing —

251
00:28:03.520 --> 00:28:05.600
because she's pleased, something enormous
has happened.

252
00:28:11.040 --> 00:28:18.080
The Ekadash Rudra is pleased, so the whole
universe is pleased,

253
00:28:18.080 --> 00:28:23.440
the whole universe is dancing — there's
rain, there's a soft,

254
00:28:24.560 --> 00:28:29.360
cool wind of the Holy Spirit permeating
the whole of nature.

255
00:28:30.000 --> 00:28:33.619
So it's very collective — it depends on
how much you're connected to her.

256
00:28:33.619 --> 00:28:33.675
Sahaja Yoga isn't a technical thing, just
the chakras —

257
00:28:33.675 --> 00:28:35.200
it's how much you're connected to her;

258
00:28:37.200 --> 00:28:52.720
Sahaja Yoga is just one aspect of her, for
us to connect to her.

259
00:28:52.720 --> 00:28:54.400
But if you're not connected,

260
00:28:54.400 --> 00:28:58.720
and you just treat it like a photo of Shri
Mataji and think, "Okay,

261
00:28:58.720 --> 00:29:05.520
I'm getting vibrations, feeling relaxed" —
then you don't really get it.

262
00:29:05.520 --> 00:29:13.440
You have to feel her in your heart, you
have to feel her in your Kundalini —

263
00:29:13.440 --> 00:29:16.080
then you're connected.

264
00:29:16.080 --> 00:29:20.960
You got your realization, but now this is
the next step.

265
00:29:20.960 --> 00:29:28.786
You can stay at that primary stage if
that's all you want, but then, one day,

266
00:29:28.786 --> 00:29:29.760
you'll slowly drift away and say,

267
00:29:29.760 --> 00:29:44.400
"I've been doing this for twenty years and
nothing has happened."

268
00:29:44.400 --> 00:29:46.320
You have a question?

269
00:29:46.320 --> 00:29:49.760
Okay, good. They are already thoughtless.
